{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"content\": \"#include <bits/stdc++.h>\\n\\nusing namespace std;\\n\\nint A[1000][1000];\\nint ps[1010][1010];\\n\\ntypedef long long ll;\\n\\nll solve(int m, int n, int k) {\\n  for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\\n    for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\\n      ps[i][j] = A[i - 1][j - 1] + ps[i][j - 1];\\n    }\\n  }\\n  ll ans = 0;\\n  #pragma omp parallel if(n > 1) reduction(+:ans)\\n  {\\n    unordered_map<ll, ll> h;\\n    #pragma omp for schedule(dynamic, 1) nowait\\n    for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\\n      for (int l = j; l <= n; l++) {\\n        h.clear();\\n        h[0] = 1;\\n        ll s = 0;\\n        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\\n          s += ps[i][l] - ps[i][j - 1];\\n          ans += h.find(s - k) != h.end() ? h[s - k] : 0;\\n          h[s]++;\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n  return ans;\\n}\\n\\nint main() {\\n  int k, m, n;\\n  cin >> k >> m >> n;\\n  memset(A, 0, sizeof A);\\n  memset(ps, 0, sizeof ps);\\n\\n  for (int i = 0; i < m; i++)\\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)\\n      cin >> A[i][j];\\n\\n  cout << solve(m, n, k) << endl;\\n  return 0;\\n}\\n\",\n      \"path\": \"src/main.cpp\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Dynamically scheduling complete starting-column tasks should balance triangular counting work across four OpenMP workers while retaining fixed-left-boundary locality and requiring at most n scheduling operations.\",\n  \"notes\": \"No commands executed. Inherits OpenMP thread settings and preserves preprocessing, counting semantics, and I/O.\",\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Use one OpenMP region with a private reusable frequency map per worker and a 64-bit answer reduction.\",\n    \"Dynamically distribute starting columns with chunk size one, preserving their complete ending-column loops.\",\n    \"Remove the redundant worksharing barrier with nowait and suppress team creation when only 